  [PASS] B2  and the exception is NOT suppressed: 2 Y J_YY = Sigma_par - Sigma_perp is O(1) at every acceleration, because J_YY ~ 1/Y supplies exactly the compensating scale   (2 Y J_YY at s = 0.1: 0.5413 (canonical) / 0.5413 (alt) -- dimensionless and order unity)
  [PASS] B3  CONSEQUENCE, stated as the load-bearing modelling step of this lane: about a background with grad(phi) != 0 the quadratic Lagrangian is L46's with the Y-term stiffness replaced by J_eff(theta) = Sigma_perp sin^2 + Sigma_par cos^2 and the xi-term stiffness by Sigma_perp = J_Y (the xi operator is (d_i d_j delta phi)^2, isotropic, and its background value vanishes)   (relative error of the reduction <= B/k <= 1e-7 across the whole band that matters)

