  [PASS] V1  IS THE CONDITION A FOOTNOTE OR A KILL?  It is a KILL.  The health condition L46 found does NOT survive on an anisotropic background: keeping grad(phi) improves the longitudinal branch and leaves the transverse branch exactly where the flat calculation put it, and BOTH fail throughout the deep-MOND regime the theory exists to explain, on both a_0 footings   (transverse unstable for s < 0.3985, longitudinal for s < 0.0994; fastest e-folding time 4.06e+02 yr at lambda ~ 0.5 pc, still 7e5 yr at lambda = 1 kpc; region r > 19.3 / 17.6 kpc for M_b = 1e11 M_sun, unbounded above)
  [PASS] V2  the deposited PASS verdicts are NOT wrong where they are evaluated, and this lane says so: the gate table's DOF-health row is correct at the external-field J_Y it uses.  What is wrong is that the row was never evaluated in the deep-MOND regime, and the condition it needed was not listed   (both footings pass at s = 1.9 and fail at s < 0.4)
  [PASS] V3  the erratum item is DISCHARGED, in the direction that costs the paper most: PAPER8's open anisotropic item is now computed, and its answer is that the flat-background threshold was not conservative -- it was exact on the softest branch   (no version-two shortening; the condition must be listed AND it must be reported as failing)
  [PASS] V4  NOTHING HERE IS CLOSED.  kappa = 1/2 remains fitted; this lane touches only the scalar sector's linear health about a WKB background, and it names its own limits: the WKB reduction is controlled by B/k <= 1e-7 (PART 3) and is not a statement about wavelengths comparable to the background scale, nor about the nonlinear endpoint of the instability   (an unstable linear mode says the background is not the endpoint; it does not say what is)

